    "report_markdown": "# Hypora run report: run_7e5d5077f853\n\n**Outcome:** a verified model.\n\n## Task\n- Objective: Predict the acute toxicity to fish (LC50) of a chemical from its molecular descriptors.\n- Target: `LC50` (regression)\n- Primary metric: `mae` (minimize)\n\n## Summary\nThe run aimed to predict acute fish toxicity from molecular descriptors. Several regression approaches were tried, and a verified ExtraTrees model was delivered.\n\n**Observations**\n- The final model's test MAE was 0.6697, with test RMSE 0.9396 and test R\u00b2 0.6013.\n- Its mean validation MAE was 0.6610, the lowest among the evaluated candidates.\n\n**Limitations**\n- A leakage candidate was flagged among the screened features and requires methodological review; learned-transform leakage screening was skipped.\n- The results use a random split and do not establish performance on other datasets or split strategies.\n\n_Written by the Reporter; every number above is filled in from stored metrics._\n\n## Final model\n- Trial `trl_3fabf62a`: ExtraTrees with shallow regularization offers a robust nonlinear ensemble for descriptor-based toxicity regression.\n- Verified: yes\n\n| Metric | Test (once) | Validation (mean) |\n|---|---|---|\n| mae | 0.6697 | 0.6610 |\n| rmse | 0.9396 | 0.9514 |\n| r2 | 0.6013 | 0.5873 |\n\n| Check | Status | Detail |\n|---|---|---|\n| allowed_features | passed | trial code received exactly the contract's allowed features |\n| split_respected | passed | random split: disjoint, complete |\n| test_labels_not_accessed | passed | every predict stage saw features and the model only |\n| output_shape | passed | one prediction per planned row, task-shaped columns |\n| finite_outputs | passed | all predictions finite and well-formed |\n| metric_recomputation | passed | recomputed metrics match the harness |\n| artifact_loads | passed | the frozen model loaded in a sandbox and predicted the test split |\n| resource_limits | passed | every stage completed inside the submitted job's limits |\n| learned_transform_leakage | skipped | static analysis of fit/predict arrives with verifier v2 (S3.C4) |\n\n## Trials\n| Trial | Kind | Status | Validation mae (mean \u00b1 std, folds) | Hypothesis |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `trl_0970bfcb` | candidate | validated | 0.6759 \u00b1 0.0497 (3) | An RBF support-vector regressor on standardized descriptors will model smooth nonlinear relationships while controlling complexity on this small dataset. |\n| `trl_3fabf62a` | candidate | verified | 0.6610 \u00b1 0.0269 (3) | ExtraTrees with shallow regularization offers a robust nonlinear ensemble for descriptor-based toxicity regression. |\n| `trl_86ee6e3a` | candidate | validated | 0.6855 \u00b1 0.0178 (3) | A nonlinear histogram gradient-boosting model can capture descriptor interactions and threshold effects better than a linear baseline. |\n| `trl_c6b410d0` | baseline | validated | 0.7267 \u00b1 0.0098 (3) | A standardized Ridge regression provides a simple linear baseline for the six molecular descriptors. |\n\n## Data\n- Split: random, 20% test, kfold_3\n- Features used: 6; excluded: none\n- Leakage screen: Leakage candidates flagged: 1 among 6 screened features; methodological review is required.\n\n## Decision and faults\n- Decision: train (approved_plan)\n\n## Run notes\n- Stage-1 placeholder (D-019): contract built by code, plan approved by policy; replaced by the Data Lead (S3.A2) and the plan gate (S3.D2).\n- The agent finished after 19 model turns, 18 tool calls; it nominated trl_3fabf62a.\n- Final candidate trl_3fabf62a: nominated by the agent.\n- Final job job_1794151702407020112_9320d5: test split scored once; verifier v1 passed.\n\n## Sources\n- `task_spec:run_7e5d5077f853.v1`\n- `profile:run_7e5d5077f853.profile.75ba1549dbac`\n- `experiment_contract:run_7e5d5077f853.v1`\n- `result:trl_3fabf62a/test`\n"
